---
title: "dynamic_field::borrow_mut (Sui Move Concepts: Dynamic Field Mutable Access)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_addr: object_addr = object.to_address()
    q_get_addr --> q_hash: hash = hash_type_and_key(object_addr, name)
    q_hash --> q_borrow_mut: field = borrow_child_object_mut(object, hash)
    q_borrow_mut --> q_check_type: verify Field type matches expected Name and Value
    q_check_type --> q_return: types match
    q_check_type --> q_abort_type: type mismatch
    q_return --> [*]: return &mut field.value

    q_abort_type --> [*]: abort - Value type mismatch

    note right of q_borrow_mut
        INV-001: Requires mutable reference to parent UID
        INV-002: Only parent object owner can obtain mutable borrow
        INV-003: Child object wrapped in dynamic field cannot be mutated directly by ID
    end note

    note right of q_return
        INV-004: Mutable reference allows in-place modification of field value
        INV-005: Modifications are reflected on-chain after transaction completes
    end note
